    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Seagate Technology Holdings plc is a public company headquartered in Singapore and traded under the ticker STX. Its website describes it as a leader in mass-capacity data storage, saying it has delivered more than four billion terabytes of capacity over the past four decades. The company says it makes storage that scales and that it aims to bring trust and integrity to innovations that depend on data.\n\nThe site frames AI as the main force behind current data growth. Seagate says AI is accelerating data growth and reshaping storage requirements, and that people and machines will create in more ways and at a faster pace as AI proliferates, producing large volumes of data. The company states it is optimizing storage for AI, with gains in capacity intended to support efficient data center architecture and buildout. It also invites organizations to evaluate their readiness and develop a storage strategy built for performance, scale, and growth.\n\nThe company's record includes a CIK identifier with the SEC, consistent with its status as a public company. No litigation, no tracked products, and no MCP servers are recorded for it.",
